{Not the best game - but very entertaining in parts.} 1. b3 Nf6 2. Bb2 d5 3. e3 Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 Bd6 6. d3 c6 7. Nbd2 Nbd7 8. Nh4 Bg6 9. h3 Qe7 10. c3 a5 11. Nxg6 fxg6 12. O-O O-O 13. c4 e5 14. e4 dxe4 15. dxe4 Nc5 16. Qc2 Ne6 17. Nf3 Nf4 18. c5 Nxe2+ $6 ({Nimzo 8 prefers} 18... Bc7) 19. Qxe2 Bxc5 20. Nxe5 Kh8 21. Nd3 Bb6 22. e5 Nh5 23. Qg4 Rf5 24. Rad1 Raf8 25. Bd4 $1 {Fritz doesn't like this, but Nimzo 8 sees more...} Rg5 26. Qe4 $2 ({Now Nimzo 8 soon sees} 26. Bxb6 $1 Rxg4 27. hxg4 Nf4 28. Nxf4 {and now not} Rxf4 $4 ({so} 28... Qxe5 29. Be3 {and White has a lot of material for the queen.}) 29. Rd8+ Rf8 30. Rxf8+ Qxf8 31. Rd1 {wins for White.}) 26... Nf6 27. exf6 $5 {Gor Blimey!} Qxe4 28. fxg7+ Kg8 29. gxf8=Q+ Kxf8 30. Nf4 $1 {Needs must when the Devil has set fire to your posterior.} Bxd4 $4 (30... Bc7 {leaves White dead lost.}) 31. Rxd4 Rxg2+ $2 ({Black is still a bit better after} 31... Qe5) 32. Kh1 $1 Rxf2+ $2 ({Black has to try} 32... Qe5 33. Kxg2 g5 $1 34. Kf3 c5 $1 {when White is only a bit better.}) 33. Rxe4 Rxf1+ 34. Kg2 Rd1 35. Rd4 Rc1 36. Rd2 Ke7 37. Nd3 Rc3 38. Ne5 Ke6 39. Nf3 h6 40. Nd4+ Kf6 41. Ne2 Re3 42. Ng3 a4 43. Kf2 Re5 44. bxa4 Ra5 45. Rd4 b5 46. Rd6+ Kg5 47. Ne4+ Kh5 48. Rxc6 Rxa4 49. Nc3 Ra3 50. Nxb5 Rxa2+ 51. Kg3 Re2 52. Nd4 Re3+ 53. Nf3 Re7 54. Rc5+ g5 55. Re5 Rg7 56. Nh2 Rb7 57. Ng4 Rb3+ 58. Re3 Rxe3+ 59. Nxe3 Kg6 60. Kf3 h5 61. Ke4 Kf6 {The scoresheet now becomes unclear in the time scramble, so the following may be incorrect.} 62. Nf1 Kg6 63. Ng3 h4 64. Nf1 g4 65. hxg4 Kg5 66. Kf3 h3 67. Kg3 h2 68. Nxh2 1-0

