1. b3 Nf6 2. Bb2 d5 3. Nf3 e6 4. c4 c5 5. cxd5 Nxd5 6. g3 Nc6 7. Bg2 Bd7 8. O-O h5 9. d4 cxd4 10. Nxd4 ({Fritz 6 is so afraid of ...h4 that it prefers} 10. Bxd4 {here.}) 10... h4 11. Nxc6 Bxc6 12. e4 (12. Nc3 $5 hxg3 13. hxg3 Qg5 14. Nxd5 Bxd5 15. e4 Bc6 16. Bc1 Qg6 {and Black has a pull, but maybe not too much.}) 12... h3 (12... Nb4 {leaving options open, is perhaps better.}) 13. Bh1 Nb4 14. Qe2 Qd3 15. Qxd3 Nxd3 16. Bd4 e5 17. Be3 Bc5 {Fritz 6 thinks White has a slight edge whereas Nimzo 8 thinks Black has.} 18. Bxc5 Nxc5 19. Nc3 Rd8 20. Rfd1 Ke7 21. Rac1 Rxd1+ 22. Rxd1 Rd8 23. Nd5+ Kf8 24. b4 Ne6 25. Bf3 $2 Ng5 (25... f5 $5 26. Nc3 (26. exf5 $4 Nd4 {wins instantly}) 26... Rd4 $1 {with advantage to Black.}) 26. Bh1 Ne6 27. Bf3 Nd4 28. Bg4 f5 $5 (28... Bxd5 29. exd5 Rxd5 30. Kf1 a5 31. bxa5 Rxa5 32. Rd2 Ra4 33. Bxh3 Rc4 34. f4 exf4 35. gxf4 {and Nimzo 8 thinks Black is quite a lot better.}) 29. Bxh3 fxe4 30. Ne3 Nf3+ 31. Kf1 (31. Kg2) 31... Nxh2+ 32. Kg1 Nf3+ 33. Kf1 Rd4 34. a3 Bb5+ 35. Kg2 Rxd1 36. Nxd1 Ne1+ 37. Kg1 Nc2 38. Nc3 Nxa3 39. Nxb5 Nxb5 40. Bg2 Nd6 41. f4 exf3 42. Bxf3 b6 43. Kf2 Ke7 44. g4 Ke6 45. Be2 a5 46. bxa5 bxa5 47. Ke3 Kd5 48. Kd3 e4+ 49. Kc3 Ke5 50. Kb3 Kd4 51. Ka4 Ke3 0-1

